<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Sélestat</h1><p class="st-meta">1292 CE – 1679 CE (approx.) · capital Sélestat</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Alsatian imperial city and Decapolis member, famous for its humanist Latin school and the library of Beatus Rhenanus.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Sélestat grew around a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> palace and the priory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-sainte-foy-selestat">Sainte-Foy</a> on the river Ill. Frederick II made it a town in 1217, and in 1292 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-of-nassau">King Adolf of Nassau</a> confirmed its liberties as an imperial city, answerable only to the emperor. In 1354 it was a founding member of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/decapolis">Decapolis</a>, the league of ten Alsatian imperial cities.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A council drawn from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guilds</a> ran the city, which prospered from wine, grain and river trade. In the later 15th century its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> school became a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a> humanism, and the scholar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beatus-rhenanus">Beatus Rhenanus</a> left his books to the town in 1547; they survive as the Humanist Library. The city remained Catholic during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Swedish troops took Sélestat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, and after 1648 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> claimed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/decapolis">Decapolis</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> had its walls razed in 1673, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaties-of-nijmegen">Treaty of Nijmegen</a> of 1679 confirmed French rule; Vauban later refortified it. It is now a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bas-rhin">Bas-Rhin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of France.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="imperial city, 1292 CE – 1679 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">imperial city</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.41%;width:7.70%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1292 CE – 1679 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>imperial city</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sélestat</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Alsatian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sélestat, Schlettstadt</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1486&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-selestat" aria-label="Free Imperial City of Sélestat on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4853 490 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free Imperial City of Sélestat lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5173 746L5918 1245M5173 746L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5918 1245h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5173 746h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5173 746h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sélestat. <a href="/atlas?year=1486&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-selestat">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

